  "test": "observe",
  "campaign_id": "npc_regression_hadrik_voss_observe",
  "turns": [
    {
      "input": "*He looks at Hadrik Voss, trying to understand what kind of person he has in front of him.*",
      "scene_location": "heartstone_square",
      "runtime_co_located": [
        "hadrik_voss"
      ],
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Hadrik Voss stands with his arms folded across his chest, his stance solid as the paving stones beneath him. The small rectangular lenses sit on the bridge of his nose, catching the daylight. He says nothing, returning the look with the same patience he might regard a warped axle brought to his shop—waiting to see what the damage is before committing to the repair.\n\nThe square's moderate traffic continues around them, a few passers-by glancing toward the tower entrance without lingering. From the direction of The Coined Lie, a woman's laugh cuts sharp and too brief, followed by the clatter of a dropped crate and a muffled oath. Hadrik does not turn toward the sound. His two stiff left fingertips remain tucked against his palm, unnoticed unless one were looking for them.\n\n\"You're staring,\" he says finally, and there is no offense in it—merely observation, the same flat tone he might use to note a hairline crack in a blade. \"Buy something, sell something, or waste someone else's daylight.\"",
